WEBVTT

00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:17,040
What is your opinion on taking low dose naltrexel?

00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:23,040
So naltrexel was initially introduced into the market.

00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,040
It's a drug.

00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:31,040
It's a drug at 50 milligrams to help get people off of more feed addiction.

00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:34,040
So I think you're talking about low dose naltrexel.

00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:37,040
You're starting off at 1.5 milligrams.

00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:42,040
Move the three milligrams and move to 4.5 milligrams.

00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:46,040
So low dose naltrexel is an immune modulator.

00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:50,040
That's really how it works.

00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:59,040
So is low dose naltrexel good for cancer as an off label drug for cancer?

00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:04,040
I have not found it to be all that useful for cancer.

00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,040
I've not seen any studies.

00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:10,040
Maybe I haven't looked lately for cancer.

00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:16,040
I found it to be extremely helpful for autoimmune patients because it could help.

00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:22,040
So with an autoimmune condition, you want to call immune response.

00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:26,040
So immune regulation is helpful.

00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:34,040
So all the end stimulates what's called T-reg production.

00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:55,040
So T-regs are a type of T cell subset called T-regulator cells that can help calm the immune response in somebody who has a hyperimmune reaction with an autoimmune disease.

00:01:55,040 --> 00:02:00,040
Now, there are some people that say that it can be a T-regulator.

00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:04,040
It can help bring up somebody's immune response if it's super suppressed.

00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:07,040
So in that case, I would say that it would be helpful.

00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:11,040
So I would say low dose naltrexel will be helpful.

00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:20,040
If somebody's voice or chemo and their white blood cell felt is extremely suppressed and they're struggling with immune suppression.

00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,040
It can help bring that up.

00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:29,040
It's not going to be an immune stimulant where it's going to help kill cancer.

00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:34,800
But it can help bring up a suppressed immune response.

00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,800
So in that case, I would say it's worth a try.

00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:43,800
But really there's not a whole lot of side effects from taking it.

00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:48,800
So I don't think there's anything wrong with giving a try.

00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:58,800
But really there's not a whole lot of side effects from taking it.

